=== layout: one-panel

# [*Steps in Three-Point Test-Cross Gene Map*]{color=red}

@body

- 1. Determine parental genotype
- Step 2\: Pick any two genes
  - completely cover up the third so it does not confuse you!!!
- 3. Determine which of the progeny are parental and non-parental genotypes
- 4. Determine the map distance between the two genes
  - 4a Sum the progeny from the non-parental genotypes
  - 4b. Divide the NP by the total progeny
  - 4c. Multiply the result by 100% to get the distance between the genes
- 5. Go to Step 2 and pick a new pair of genes until all pairs are complete
- 6. Use all the gene distances to determine the order of the genes.
  - largest distance are furthest away and on the ends

=== layout: section

# Quick Method to Determine Gene Order

=== layout: one-panel

# [*Quick Gene Order Method for Three-Point Test-Cross*]{color=#55215B}

@body

- Step 1. Determine parental genotypes
  - Two genotypes with most progeny
- Step 2\: Determine double crossover (DCO) genotypes
  - Two genotypes with fewest progeny
- Step 3. Compare parental genotypes with double crossover genotypes to see which single gene flipped in the DCO
- Step 4\: Determine the gene order given that the flipped gene is the middle gene.

