# How many different ways to write order of three genes A B C?

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *How many different ways to write order of A B C*

@body

- A B C &#8596; C B A
- A C B &#8596; B C A
- B A C &#8596; C A B
  - only three, if flips are the same gene order

- A B C

- B A C

- C B A

- C A B

- A B C

- B A C

- The answer is
- 3

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Possible Gene Orders*

@body

- With three genes there are always three options for gene order\:
- ABC, ACB, or BAC
- Note\:
  - It only depends on which gene is in the middle
  - ABC &#8596; CBA || ACB &#8596; BCA || BAC &#8596; CAB
- Since these are chromosomes, the reverse order of the gene is the same/does not matter

- A B C

- B A C

- C B A

- C A B

- A B C

- B A C

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *How many different ways to write order of A B C D*

@body

- A B C D &#8596; D C B A
- A B D C &#8596; C D B A
- A C B D &#8596; D B C A
- A C D B &#8596; B D C A
- A D B C &#8596; C B D A
- A D C B &#8596; B C D A

- B A C D &#8596; D C A B
- B A D C &#8596; C D A B
- B C A D &#8596; D A C B
- B D A C &#8596; C A D B
- C A B D &#8596; D B A C
- C B A D &#8596; D A B C

![Slide image 9](assets/lect08f-3_point_testcross_textbook/image_009.svg)

- [12; This is just too many for a quiz or exam!]{color=#009999}

